    "title": "Character.ai Open-Sourced an AI Judge for Video Slop",
    "source_text": "Character.AI open-sourced JudgeJudy, a multimodal evaluation framework aimed at AI video \"slop\"\n\nVideo generation quality has raced ahead with models like Kling, Seedance, Veo and Sora, but evaluation has lagged: frame-level tools such as CLIP score and LPIPS check whether a single frame matches its prompt or drifts from the next one, and say nothing about whether a clip actually told the intended story, kept a character consistent across shots, obeyed physics or synced its audio to the action. JudgeJudy, released under an MIT license, combines AI judges with custom rubrics, automated metrics and human scoring across text, image, audio and video, including temporal consistency (frame-to-frame SSIM) and CLIP-temporal metrics, with provider support for Seedance, WAN, Veo 3 and Sora 2. This matters because generation is now effectively free compared to studio costs while judging quality still requires a human — the bottleneck has moved from making video to knowing which video is worth keeping.",
    "source_path": null,
